    "media:imagetext": "1\nJuly 24, 1949\nDesr Family,\nI think that my lest letter covered this trip as far as Japan. We are now\nflying from Karachi, Pakistan to Demeseus, Syria - an eight-hour, non-stop jump\nof over 2,000 miles. From Japan we flew to Okinawa and Hongkong. A short trip\nto Canton, three tripe to Manila and one back to Tokyo, then on to Bangkok where\nI stayed four days.\nThat is a most interesting and pleasant place. The temples\nare megnificent and the people so courteous and friendly that it is refreshing.\nEveryone seems so glad to see you and even the taxi drivers say \"thank you\" in\nmarked contrast with the sullen gas jockeys of Manhattan. I saw all the Cabinet\nMinisters and the Prime Minister.\nAlso had a private, for-me-only tour through\nthe Royal Palace accompanied by an under Secretary who knew the whole history\nand spoke perfect English. The Enerald Buddha temple is one of the great sights\nof the world. It and other temples are elosed to the publie now because the\nPalace grounds were chosen by the leaders of the most recent \"coups d'etat\" as\nthe bese of their military operations, and they do not propose to be thrown out\nthe way they got in. You will remember that the young king was mysteriously\nmurdered a few years ago. His body was put in a big earthenvare jar and there\nit must remain until his younger brother returns from Switzerland.\nseems to prefer his safe, comfortable Tyrolean bonnet rather than the fourteen\ncarat dangerous hardware\nwhich was shot off the unhappy head of his lete older\nApparently he has no intention of coming home.\nSo, the funeral pyre\non which the body of the late King will be cremated stands weathered and dila-\npidated outside the Palace grounds.\nWe have just flown over the Texas Company refinery on Bahrein Island. A\nfloating pipeline runs out to sea where five tankers were taking on oil.\nJust\nbeyond Behrein is enother great oil producing center - Dhahran, within sight\nof which there are seven fields, esch of which is lerger than any other in the\nThe Anglo-Irenian pipeline is being built (by Leif Sverdrup of St. Louis)\nfrom here to Beirut. It is just possible that while the Russian dog is barking\nat Berlin, the Russian dog that doesn't bark - but may bite - is lurking silent\nin this vest desert space below us.\nAt Menila I met a Siamese-Chinese named Chulind who gave me a Chinese\nLuncheon perty at Bangkok followed by a pienie boatride on the river. It reelly\nwas a great treat. The river traffic is much like Canton where people are born,\nlive and die on boats.\nle stopped at the Temple of the Dawn and elimbed up\nsome stairs to get a view of Bangkok.\nI stayed st the Trocadero Hotel. During my first night there my uneasy\nsleep on a concrete msttress with pillow to mateh was broken by the most terrifie\nyowling of dogs which were being killed in a cleanup campaign. Fortunately they\ngot most of them the first night, beeause the din was not so bad on subsequent\nYou know, in British sphere countries they have three initial designations:\n\"H.E.\" which is \"His Excellency\", and when they get \u0026 little higher up on the\nATEIISIAOS",
